(a) It shall be unlawful for any person to sleep, lie down, to reside upon, or to store personal property in any park, in any cemetery, upon any sidewalk, or in or upon any public property of the city.
(b) It shall be unlawful for any person to use any public park, cemetery, public sidewalk, or public property for living accommodations or for camping, except in areas specifically designated for such use.
(c) It shall be unlawful for any person other than the owner, tenant, employee, or other person with permission from the owner, to camp, sleep, reside, store personal property upon, or lie down outside upon any private property without the owner's permission to do so.
(d) Notwithstanding the provisions of this section, this section shall not apply to the following:
(1) Persons sitting or lying down as a result of a medical emergency;
(2) Persons sitting in wheelchairs while using parks, sidewalks or other public places;
(3) Persons sitting down while attending parades for which valid permits have been issued;
(4) Persons sitting down while patronizing outdoor cafes;
(5) Persons sitting on chairs or benches supplied by a public agency or by an abutting private property owner; provided, however, that such exception shall not apply to persons sleeping, lying down, residing upon, or storing personal property upon such chairs or benches;
(6) Persons sitting down or lying down while attending sporting events, performances, festivals and concerts taking place in any park, or upon any street or sidewalk where such event is authorized by the city;
(7) Children under the age of 13 years sleeping in parks while being carried by or accompanied by another person over such age, or while sitting or lying in a baby stroller or carriage;
(8) Persons offering the sale of merchandise, food, vegetables, fruit, produce and similar items from the sidewalk in front of a business where such sale is otherwise authorized by the City Code.
(e) A person convicted of violating this Code section, or a person entering a plea of guilty or nolo contendre to a violation of this Code section, shall be punished as provided in section 1-8 of the City Code. Each day that a person violates this Code section shall be considered to be a separate offense. In no event shall a violation of this Code section be considered or held to be a lesser included offense of the offense of loitering as provided in section 62-114 of the City Code.
(Ord. No. O-09-07-21, 7-23-2009)

